1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,600
Everyone who buys from your store is a customer, and some of them are businesses.

2
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:09,831
This video shows how the Customers and Companies modules keep track of who

3
00:00:09,831 --> 00:00:13,268
they are, how to reach them and what they are owed, and how

4
00:00:13,268 --> 00:00:15,330
to sell to a business on account.

5
00:00:19,930 --> 00:00:22,783
Everyone who buys from your store is a customer:

6
00:00:22,783 --> 00:00:26,641
a person or a business, with an account on your site or as a guest.

7
00:00:26,641 --> 00:00:30,128
To serve them you need to know how to address them, where to

8
00:00:30,128 --> 00:00:33,510
send their orders, and whether they want to hear from you.

9
00:00:34,260 --> 00:00:36,324
Businesses buy differently.

10
00:00:36,324 --> 00:00:41,390
Several people buy for one company, it often pays an invoice later, expects

11
00:00:41,390 --> 00:00:45,830
its own prices, and wants a manager to approve the larger orders.

12
00:00:46,580 --> 00:00:51,183
Shoppers expect to keep an address book, to be rewarded when they come

13
00:00:51,183 --> 00:00:55,240
back, and to ask what you hold on them, or to have it erased.

14
00:00:55,990 --> 00:01:01,150
The Customers and Companies modules cover all of this from one place in the admin.

15
00:01:05,350 --> 00:01:08,356
A customer record keeps what your store needs:

16
00:01:08,356 --> 00:01:12,749
how to address them, their company and tax id, their address book, and

17
00:01:12,749 --> 00:01:14,830
whether they accept marketing.

18
00:01:15,580 --> 00:01:19,533
The sign in, the password and the email stay on the user account.

19
00:01:19,533 --> 00:01:23,819
A customer with an account gets their record the first time they order.

20
00:01:23,819 --> 00:01:28,440
A guest who checks out without an account gets a guest customer of their own.

21
00:01:29,190 --> 00:01:33,955
A company is a business you sell to, with its buyers, payment terms,

22
00:01:33,955 --> 00:01:36,530
shipping locations and price list.

23
00:01:37,280 --> 00:01:42,962
Store Credit, Loyalty Points, Referrals and Checkout details are separate features you turn

24
00:01:42,962 --> 00:01:47,063
on, to reward customers who come back and to ask buyers for your

25
00:01:47,063 --> 00:01:48,820
own details at checkout.

26
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:54,917
Open Commerce, Customers.

27
00:01:54,917 --> 00:02:00,716
The people and businesses that bought from you are listed with the most recently active first.

28
00:02:00,716 --> 00:02:04,427
A badge marks a guest or a business, and each row shows an

29
00:02:04,427 --> 00:02:06,920
email and when they were last active.

30
00:02:07,383 --> 00:02:11,183
Type the start of a name, a company or an email in the

31
00:02:11,183 --> 00:02:14,603
search box and press Enter to find one customer.

32
00:02:15,066 --> 00:02:18,343
The list beside the count narrows what is shown:

33
00:02:18,343 --> 00:02:23,502
customers With an account, Guests, Businesses, Disabled ones, or All customers.

34
00:02:23,502 --> 00:02:27,326
Choose Businesses to see the companies that buy from you.

35
00:02:31,497 --> 00:02:35,399
To add a customer you deal with outside the site, such as someone

36
00:02:35,399 --> 00:02:37,927
who orders by phone, click Add customer.

37
00:02:38,379 --> 00:02:43,015
Choose the Kind, Person or Business, and type the first and last name.

38
00:02:43,015 --> 00:02:46,370
The Display name is how the store addresses them.

39
00:02:46,370 --> 00:02:48,749
Leave it empty to use their name.

40
00:02:49,203 --> 00:02:52,365
A business also has a Company and a Tax id.

41
00:02:52,365 --> 00:02:56,561
Tick Exempt from tax for a reseller or a charity you hold a

42
00:02:56,561 --> 00:02:59,917
certificate for, and note Why they are exempt.

43
00:02:59,917 --> 00:03:03,467
When they check out signed in, no tax is charged.

44
00:03:03,467 --> 00:03:05,403
A guest is always taxed.

45
00:03:05,854 --> 00:03:09,092
Add an Email and a Phone so you can reach them.

46
00:03:09,092 --> 00:03:13,369
Tick Accepts marketing only when they agreed to news and offers.

47
00:03:13,369 --> 00:03:16,364
Order and payment messages are always sent.

48
00:03:16,816 --> 00:03:17,795
Click Save.

49
00:03:17,795 --> 00:03:23,263
The customer opens with their Orders, Store credit, Addresses and Privacy sections below.

50
00:03:23,263 --> 00:03:28,789
The Status field lets you mark a customer Disabled when you stop doing business with them.

51
00:03:28,789 --> 00:03:30,516
They keep their history.

52
00:03:34,692 --> 00:03:37,418
Open a customer to see their address book.

53
00:03:37,418 --> 00:03:42,529
One address can be the default billing address and one the default shipping address.

54
00:03:42,529 --> 00:03:45,992
They are the ones offered first when the customer buys.

55
00:03:46,447 --> 00:03:47,827
Click Add address.

56
00:03:47,827 --> 00:03:51,967
Choose the Country first, because the rest of the form follows it.

57
00:03:52,421 --> 00:03:57,796
Choose United Kingdom, and the form asks for a Post town and a Postal code.

58
00:03:57,796 --> 00:04:03,171
Choose United States, and it asks for a State, from a list, and a ZIP code.

59
00:04:03,622 --> 00:04:07,999
Fill in the street and the city, choose the State, and enter the ZIP code.

60
00:04:07,999 --> 00:04:12,486
Give the address a Label such as Warehouse, tick Default shipping address to

61
00:04:12,486 --> 00:04:15,332
make it the one offered first, and click Save.

62
00:04:15,783 --> 00:04:19,964
The address is checked against its country, so a postal code has to

63
00:04:19,964 --> 00:04:21,739
look like that country's.

64
00:04:21,739 --> 00:04:26,034
Orders keep their own copy of an address, so changing or deleting one

65
00:04:26,034 --> 00:04:27,923
never changes a past order.

66
00:04:32,127 --> 00:04:35,544
Open a customer with an account, such as Jamie Chen.

67
00:04:35,544 --> 00:04:39,728
Store credit is money the store owes a customer, such as a refund

68
00:04:39,728 --> 00:04:41,201
you give as credit.

69
00:04:41,201 --> 00:04:44,147
It pays toward their next orders, after tax.

70
00:04:44,605 --> 00:04:49,497
Under Store credit, enter an Amount, check the Currency, and give a Reason,

71
00:04:49,497 --> 00:04:51,188
such as Late delivery.

72
00:04:51,188 --> 00:04:52,335
Click Change.

73
00:04:52,786 --> 00:04:57,441
The balance updates, and the latest changes are listed with when, what, the

74
00:04:57,441 --> 00:04:59,625
change and the balance after it.

75
00:04:59,625 --> 00:05:02,038
A negative amount takes credit away.

76
00:05:02,038 --> 00:05:06,176
A guest cannot have credit, because it is spent when they sign in.

77
00:05:06,650 --> 00:05:09,207
Loyalty points work the same way.

78
00:05:09,207 --> 00:05:14,322
Under Rewards, enter the Points to give, and a Reason, and click Change.

79
00:05:14,322 --> 00:05:18,190
The section shows the points and what they are worth.

80
00:05:22,394 --> 00:05:25,123
Open Settings, Commerce, Customers.

81
00:05:25,123 --> 00:05:30,448
Billing address at checkout decides whether the Contact step asks for one:

82
00:05:30,448 --> 00:05:32,644
Optional, Required, or Off.

83
00:05:33,125 --> 00:05:39,302
Under Privacy, Erase inactive guests after and Anonymize guest orders after say how

84
00:05:39,302 --> 00:05:42,702
many months you keep guests' personal data.

85
00:05:42,702 --> 00:05:44,645
Enter zero to keep it.

86
00:05:45,122 --> 00:05:50,303
Settings, Address suggestions has a field for a Google Places API key.

87
00:05:50,303 --> 00:05:55,688
With a key, every address form suggests addresses as the street is typed.

88
00:05:55,688 --> 00:05:59,642
Without one, shoppers type their address themselves.

89
00:06:00,096 --> 00:06:03,510
Settings, Commerce, Rewards sets up loyalty points.

90
00:06:03,510 --> 00:06:07,883
Give the program a name that buyers see, the Points per unit spent,

91
00:06:07,883 --> 00:06:11,476
What a point is worth, and the Fewest points to spend.

92
00:06:11,972 --> 00:06:17,392
Settings, Commerce, Referrals gives every signed-in customer a link to share.

93
00:06:17,392 --> 00:06:23,008
Choose What a friend gets, a single-use coupon code, and What the customer gets:

94
00:06:23,008 --> 00:06:26,012
nothing, store credit or loyalty points.

95
00:06:26,491 --> 00:06:32,122
Set the Least a friend's first order spends, so rewards go only to real purchases.

96
00:06:32,122 --> 00:06:36,984
A customer is rewarded once per friend, never for their own order, and

97
00:06:36,984 --> 00:06:40,631
the reward is taken back if that order is canceled.

98
00:06:44,801 --> 00:06:47,153
People can ask what you hold on them.

99
00:06:47,153 --> 00:06:49,669
Open the customer and scroll to Privacy.

100
00:06:49,669 --> 00:06:53,882
Download data gives you a file with everything the store holds on them,

101
00:06:53,882 --> 00:06:55,961
to send to the person who asked.

102
00:06:56,419 --> 00:07:01,810
Erase personal data removes their name, email, phone and addresses, and the personal

103
00:07:01,810 --> 00:07:03,607
details of their orders.

104
00:07:03,607 --> 00:07:08,519
The orders themselves stay, because your accounts and tax records need them.

105
00:07:08,972 --> 00:07:11,161
Let's erase Avery Stone.

106
00:07:11,161 --> 00:07:14,445
Click Erase personal data, and confirm.

107
00:07:14,445 --> 00:07:16,342
It cannot be undone.

108
00:07:16,804 --> 00:07:22,305
The customer now says that their personal data was erased, and can no longer be edited.

109
00:07:22,305 --> 00:07:27,864
Each download and erasure is listed under Privacy, with when it happened and who did it.

110
00:07:32,076 --> 00:07:37,474
A signed-in customer manages their own details on the Account details page of their account.

111
00:07:37,474 --> 00:07:41,164
I buy for says whether they buy for Myself or for A business.

112
00:07:41,164 --> 00:07:45,019
They edit their name, the name we call them by, their phone, and

113
00:07:45,019 --> 00:07:47,223
whether they want news and offers.

114
00:07:47,223 --> 00:07:49,646
Their email is changed on the account.

115
00:07:50,185 --> 00:07:52,772
Addresses lists their address book.

116
00:07:52,772 --> 00:07:57,505
They add, edit and delete addresses the same way you do in the admin.

117
00:07:57,961 --> 00:08:03,344
With Store Credit on, Store credit shows what they have and how it changed.

118
00:08:03,344 --> 00:08:07,131
With Loyalty Points on, Rewards shows their points.

119
00:08:07,582 --> 00:08:11,537
With Referrals on, Refer a friend shows their link to share.

120
00:08:11,537 --> 00:08:16,152
A friend who opens it can get a discount, and the customer is rewarded.

121
00:08:20,334 --> 00:08:24,320
A price list gives the companies on it their own prices.

122
00:08:24,320 --> 00:08:28,114
Open Commerce, Price lists, and click Add price list.

123
00:08:28,566 --> 00:08:30,383
Name it, such as Wholesale.

124
00:08:30,383 --> 00:08:32,310
Only your staff see the name.

125
00:08:32,310 --> 00:08:37,376
Percentage off everything else gives every product that is not on the list a discount.

126
00:08:37,906 --> 00:08:40,781
Under Prices by S.K.U., enter a S.K.U.

127
00:08:40,781 --> 00:08:44,113
and its price on each line, apart by a comma.

128
00:08:44,113 --> 00:08:47,576
Paste them from a spreadsheet if you have many.

129
00:08:48,033 --> 00:08:49,031
Click Save.

130
00:08:49,031 --> 00:08:53,143
A product on the list costs its price there, and any other costs

131
00:08:53,143 --> 00:08:55,316
your price less the percentage.

132
00:08:55,316 --> 00:08:59,193
A buyer always pays the lower of the list's price and yours.

133
00:09:03,397 --> 00:09:05,257
Open Commerce, Companies.

134
00:09:05,257 --> 00:09:08,197
The businesses you sell to are listed here.

135
00:09:08,197 --> 00:09:09,637
Click Add company.

136
00:09:10,090 --> 00:09:14,046
Enter its Name, a Tax or VAT number that is printed on its

137
00:09:14,046 --> 00:09:17,940
invoices, and a Billing email that gets its invoices too.

138
00:09:18,390 --> 00:09:22,398
Under Buyers, enter the User name or email of each person.

139
00:09:22,398 --> 00:09:24,714
They need a user account first.

140
00:09:24,714 --> 00:09:26,467
Choose Buyer or Admin.

141
00:09:26,467 --> 00:09:30,725
An admin sees all of the company's orders and approves orders.

142
00:09:30,725 --> 00:09:35,170
Give a buyer an Order limit if their bigger orders need approval.

143
00:09:35,628 --> 00:09:40,095
Under Payment terms, Net days says that what the company does not pay

144
00:09:40,095 --> 00:09:43,252
at checkout is invoiced, due in that many days.

145
00:09:43,252 --> 00:09:45,814
Deposit is the part paid at checkout.

146
00:09:45,814 --> 00:09:49,328
Credit limit is the most the company may owe at once.

147
00:09:49,820 --> 00:09:54,849
A Monthly budget sends the orders beyond it in a month to an admin for approval.

148
00:09:54,849 --> 00:09:59,352
Tick Buyers give a purchase order number to require one on every order,

149
00:09:59,352 --> 00:10:01,340
and print it on the invoice.

150
00:10:01,790 --> 00:10:06,237
Choose the company's Price list, so its buyers pay Wholesale prices.

151
00:10:06,237 --> 00:10:10,684
Under Locations, name a place it has orders shipped to, such as Head

152
00:10:10,684 --> 00:10:12,847
office, and enter the address.

153
00:10:12,847 --> 00:10:15,130
Its buyers pick one at checkout.

154
00:10:15,581 --> 00:10:21,108
The On switch lets you turn a company off, so its buyers buy for themselves again.

155
00:10:21,108 --> 00:10:22,175
Click Save.

156
00:10:22,175 --> 00:10:24,561
The company appears in the list.

157
00:10:28,761 --> 00:10:33,485
Two settings send an order to the company's admins before it can be paid:

158
00:10:33,485 --> 00:10:37,192
a buyer's Order limit, and the company's Monthly budget.

159
00:10:37,192 --> 00:10:40,061
An admin's own orders never need approval.

160
00:10:40,811 --> 00:10:45,469
At checkout, a company buyer gets a Company step after shipping, where they

161
00:10:45,469 --> 00:10:47,654
enter the purchase order number.

162
00:10:47,654 --> 00:10:52,311
If the order needs approval, the step says why and offers Ask for approval.

163
00:10:53,061 --> 00:10:55,243
The company's admins are emailed.

164
00:10:55,243 --> 00:10:59,439
An admin approves or rejects the order from the Company page of their

165
00:10:59,439 --> 00:11:02,236
account, and can leave a note for the buyer.

166
00:11:02,236 --> 00:11:04,361
The buyer is emailed either way.

167
00:11:05,111 --> 00:11:07,621
An approved order offers Pay now.

168
00:11:07,621 --> 00:11:09,874
A rejected order is canceled.

169
00:11:09,874 --> 00:11:15,601
What the company owes on account is shown on its Company page, and in Transactions.

170
00:11:19,899 --> 00:11:24,691
Punchout lets a company's procurement system, such as S.A.P., open your store.

171
00:11:24,691 --> 00:11:28,627
The buyer fills a cart, and it goes back to their system, where

172
00:11:28,627 --> 00:11:30,509
it is approved and ordered.

173
00:11:30,970 --> 00:11:37,517
On the company, tick Its procurement system shops here by punchout, and enter the Punchout buyer:

174
00:11:37,517 --> 00:11:42,030
a user who only buys for the company, and is listed under Buyers.

175
00:11:42,483 --> 00:11:47,809
After you save, the company's punchout key and punchout address are shown once.

176
00:11:47,809 --> 00:11:51,255
Give them to the company to set up in its system.

177
00:11:51,255 --> 00:11:55,703
To stop a key working, tick Make a new key, or turn punchout off.

178
00:11:59,903 --> 00:12:01,994
A shop that sells to the public:

179
00:12:01,994 --> 00:12:07,167
guests check out quickly, and customers with accounts keep their addresses, their points

180
00:12:07,167 --> 00:12:08,763
and their store credit.

181
00:12:09,513 --> 00:12:10,702
A wholesaler:

182
00:12:10,702 --> 00:12:15,270
set up each reseller as a company, with a Wholesale price list, net

183
00:12:15,270 --> 00:12:19,713
thirty payment terms, and a purchase order number on every order.

184
00:12:20,463 --> 00:12:21,716
A buying team:

185
00:12:21,716 --> 00:12:26,289
give each buyer an order limit and the company a monthly budget, so

186
00:12:26,289 --> 00:12:28,983
a manager approves the larger orders.

187
00:12:29,733 --> 00:12:31,212
A privacy request:

188
00:12:31,212 --> 00:12:35,894
find the customer, download their data to send to them, or erase their

189
00:12:35,894 --> 00:12:38,543
personal data and keep your accounts.

190
00:12:40,543 --> 00:12:45,037
The Customers and Companies modules keep everyone who buys from you in one

191
00:12:45,037 --> 00:12:48,463
place, and let you sell to a business on its own terms.

192
00:12:48,463 --> 00:12:49,923
Thanks for watching.

